  "subject": "Before her boyfriend leaves for a two-year posting in Toronto, a woman breaks their finished 1,000-piece world-map jigsaw down the middle; he takes the half with Hong Kong, she keeps the half with Toronto, and he carries his home rebuilt in a pizza box.",
  "caption": "Cantonese fado, Lisbon tavern-room style. Portuguese guitar with shimmering tremolo runs answering the voice, nylon-string classical guitar in steady bass-and-chord accompaniment, acoustic bass guitar on the roots, bowed cello sustaining under the chorus. Intimate tavern-room recording, natural reverb, close acoustic strings. Female mezzo-soprano, full-voiced and declamatory in the fadista manner, long held vowels, clearly sung melody on every line. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 88 BPM, D minor. Longing but steadfast, warm and patient. No drums, no synths, no autotune, no rap, no electric guitar distortion, no pop beat.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n一千塊拼圖 拼咗三個禮拜\n世界攤滿成張枱\n你話下個月 去多倫多\n我話好 跟住坐低\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我將佢由中間分開\n一邊香港 一邊多倫多\n\n[Chorus]\n你拎住香港嗰半\n我留低多倫多嗰半\n你嗰半拼圖有我\n我嗰半拼圖有你\n\n[Verse]\n你揀咗個空薄餅盒\n細心將香港放入去\n你話過海關 冇人會問\n入面係我哋個家\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我將多倫多擺喺書桌\n對住盞燈 慢慢睇\n\n[Chorus]\n你拎住香港嗰半\n我留低多倫多嗰半\n你嗰半拼圖有我\n我嗰半拼圖有你\n\n[Verse]\n兩年好長 我知\n每晚我望住嗰半\n塔頂缺咗一格\n我唔補 等你嚟補\n\n[Bridge]\n等你返嚟嗰日\n我哋將兩邊對返齊\n邊度有條縫\n邊度就係我哋\n\n[Chorus]\n你拎住香港嗰半\n我留低多倫多嗰半\n你嗰半拼圖有我\n等你返嚟 我嗰半有你\n\n[Outro]\n你嗰半有我\n我嗰半有你",
